.TH THUMTOO-SERVE 1 "2026-10-23" "thumtoo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thumtoo-serve \- serve a thumtoo cache read-only over HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thumtoo-serve
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Exposes the locations, metadata and stored tiles of a thumtoo cache over
HTTP for remote viewers (a thumtoo Client opened with
.BR Client::open_remote ,
e.g. galapix with
.BR "\-\-thumtoo\-cache http://HOST:PORT/?token=..." ).
Nothing is generated: a tile that is not in the cache answers 404. The cache
is opened read-only and may be in use by other programs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " DIR"
Cache root (default \fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumtoo\fR or \fI~/.cache/thumtoo\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " HOST:PORT"
Bind address (default 127.0.0.1:8080).
.TP
.BI \-\-allow\-prefix " URI"
Only expose locations whose URI starts with \fIURI\fR. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
Read the access token from \fIFILE\fR; create it (mode 0600) with a random
token if it does not exist.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auth
Never require a token.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Request threads (default 8).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log every request to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
A loopback bind needs no token. Any other bind requires one: a random token
per start unless \fB\-\-token\-file\fR is given. The URL printed at startup
carries it as \fB?token=\fR; clients may also send
.B "Authorization: Bearer TOKEN"
or the \fBthumtoo_token\fR cookie.
.PP
There is no TLS. To encrypt, tunnel the port (\fBssh \-L\fR, Tailscale,
WireGuard) or put a reverse proxy in front.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thumtoo (7),
.BR thumtoo-status (1)
.PP
docs/REMOTE.md in the thumtoo sources describes the routes.
